   {
    "id": "kifune-shrine",
    "category": "shrine",
    "name": {
     "en": "Kifune Shrine (Izumi)",
     "ja": "貴船神社（和泉）"
    },
    "about": {
     "en": "An outlying shrine of Izumi Kumano, enshrining the rain-bringing dragon kami of Kyoto's Kifune Shrine. Its pond, said never to run dry, was where villagers prayed for rain and is said to have given Izumi, 'spring', its name; it dried up around 1965.",
     "ja": "和泉熊野神社の境外末社で、京都の貴船神社の雨の龍神をまつる。涸れることがないといわれた池は雨乞いの場で、「和泉」の地名の由来ともいわれる。池は1965年ごろに涸れた。"
    },
